{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794398989,"nonce":"ld8FKysNCk1KGzJo/5mBvZrjkrs=","message":"Narrowed: this is the AIR interpreter arms over-retaining, not roots or closures.\n\n- `ASH_AIR=off` (flat-opcode interpreter) gives 200 on the original program in both `--mode interp` and the default hybrid. The default arm and `ASH_AIR=v2-serialize` both give 10200.\n- ASH_GC_STATS: interp finalizers registered 11250, queued 0; jit queued 10248. ASH_GC_DEBUG_ROOTS: \"root slots\" keeps growing only because the abstracts never die; the thread-stack line is what grows by ~81 KB per round (89, 170, 252, 333, 414 KB), one more dead 2000-element array per round. With the post-loop code removed it stays at 8 KB.\n- Static shape matters: deleting the loop that calls `Native.call_kept(held[i], 1)` AFTER the measured line (so `held` is not read again) makes the interp result 200. Cutting everything after the first println leaves the leak.\n- No native code or root is needed. Native-free program, `hl.Gc.stats().currentMemory` growth after five rounds of `churn(2000); garbage(); hl.Gc.major()`: default arm 64 KB when `held` is not read afterwards, 640 KB when it is (`for (i in 0...held.length) sum += held[i][0]`); `ASH_AIR=off` 64 KB for both.\n\n```haxe\nclass P {\n\tstatic function box(i:Int):Array\u003cInt\u003e return [i, i * 2];\n\tstatic function make(count:Int):Array\u003cArray\u003cInt\u003e\u003e return [for (i in 0...count) box(i)];\n\tstatic function garbage() { var junk = []; for (i in 0...20000) junk.push([i, i + 1, i + 2]); }\n\tstatic function churn(count:Int) { make(count); }\n\tstatic function main() {\n\t\tvar held = make(200);\n\t\tvar base = hl.Gc.stats().currentMemory;\n\t\tfor (round in 0...5) { churn(2000); garbage(); hl.Gc.major(); }\n\t\tSys.println('grown after 5 rounds: ${Std.int((hl.Gc.stats().currentMemory - base) / 1024)} KB');\n\t\tvar sum = 0;                       // present: 640 KB; removed: 64 KB\n\t\tfor (i in 0...held.length) sum += held[i][0];\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nSo a dead callee result stays reachable from the AIR interpreter's value storage or stack while the caller's frame is live, and which values stay depends on the caller's shape. The finalizer case is that over-retention made permanent: a rooted abstract that is never finalized never calls `hl_remove_root`.\n\nNot yet found: which storage holds the stale values. Next step is to attribute the thread-stack claim to an address and compare it against the AIR value frames.","files":null}]}